  "id": "merge-master-mike-WP-JAILHOLLOW1-hollow-negative-control-rejection",
  "intent": "AgentOps hardening 2a (HOLLOW CONTROLS, HIGH/integrity): the negative-control jail provisions python3+git but not pytest (site-packages are excluded and the venv interpreter is swapped for the base executable), so a `python -m pytest` control exits 1 on 'No module named pytest' and collides with the expected non-zero exit \u2014 recorded PASSED without running. Fix run_negative_control to (a) prove a `python -m MODULE` control's module imports under the identical confinement before trusting its exit code, and (b) reject a passing non-zero python control whose output is an interpreter/setup import failure. Failing-first regression tests included.",
